            <dashboardComponent>
                <autoselectColumnsFromReport>true</autoselectColumnsFromReport>
                <componentType>RichText</componentType>
                <dashboardComponentContents>
                    <richTextContent>[{\&amp;quot;attributes\&amp;quot;:{\&amp;quot;underline\&amp;quot;:true,\&amp;quot;color\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;#0d33b6\&amp;quot;,\&amp;quot;size\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;20px\&amp;quot;,\&amp;quot;bold\&amp;quot;:true},\&amp;quot;insert\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;Note regarding Sales Group Undefined\&amp;quot;},{\&amp;quot;attributes\&amp;quot;:{\&amp;quot;color\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;#0d33b6\&amp;quot;,\&amp;quot;size\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;20px\&amp;quot;},\&amp;quot;insert\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;: A value of Undefined disables any CRM user from adding new opportunities to the Account Record. Any old Opportunities still show associated if prior to the sales group change. Sales Group of Undefined is our current \&amp;#39;default\&amp;#39; when a user is requesting a new Account request. Many sales cloud app dependent process\&amp;#39; don\&amp;#39;t require opportunity mngmt and thus create account requests for undefined sales group such as: IPA, IPS, B2B Entitlement, Co-Marketing Active.\&amp;quot;},{\&amp;quot;attributes\&amp;quot;:{\&amp;quot;align\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;left\&amp;quot;},\&amp;quot;insert\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;\\n\&amp;quot;}]</richTextContent>
                </dashboardComponentContents>
                <groupingSortProperties/>
            </dashboardComponent>
            <rowIndex>28</rowIndex>
            <rowSpan>4</rowSpan>
        </dashboardGridComponents>
        <dashboardGridComponents>
            <colSpan>12</colSpan>
            <columnIndex>0</columnIndex>
            <dashboardComponent>
                <autoselectColumnsFromReport>true</autoselectColumnsFromReport>
                <componentType>RichText</componentType>
                <dashboardComponentContents>
                    <richTextContent>[{\&amp;quot;attributes\&amp;quot;:{\&amp;quot;underline\&amp;quot;:true,\&amp;quot;color\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;#6400b6\&amp;quot;,\&amp;quot;size\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;20px\&amp;quot;,\&amp;quot;bold\&amp;quot;:true},\&amp;quot;insert\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;Note regarding Account Owner = Uncovered Account\&amp;quot;},{\&amp;quot;attributes\&amp;quot;:{\&amp;quot;color\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;#6400b6\&amp;quot;,\&amp;quot;size\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;20px\&amp;quot;},\&amp;quot;insert\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;: Other Sales Cloud applications use of Accounts in Sales CRM do not require an Account Owner; such as IPA Account, Co-Marketing Active, PSG Downstream, Partner consumption, and other use cases. These drive a good portion of the Uncovered Owner accounts but not all. A Intel Led Sales Group account may also currently show Uncovered Owner if owner has changed or WIP being assigned. Uncovered Account Owner DOES NOT mean the account is no longer in use\&amp;quot;},{\&amp;quot;attributes\&amp;quot;:{\&amp;quot;align\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;left\&amp;quot;},\&amp;quot;insert\&amp;quot;:\&amp;quot;\\n\&amp;quot;}]</richTextContent>
